Blightfire Moors [zone=432]\n- Direwind Cliffs [zone=441]\n- Frostcrypt: Raid Instance #2 [zone=454]\n- Goru`kar Mesa [zone=434]\n- Icefall Glacier [zone=438]\n- Stone Hive [zone=433]\n- Sunderock Springs [zone=435]\n- The Steppes [zone=437]\n- Valdeholm [zone=439]\n- Valdeholm: Udengar the Traitor [zone=459]\n- Vergalid Mines [zone=440]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Ambersnout the Aberration [npc=23680]\n- Beltron the Shade King [npc=23932]\n- Corpsetender Xacine [npc=22719]\n- Direwind Gust [npc=22773]\n- Doomfount [npc=22755]\n- Dranadune [npc=22763]\n- Guardian of the Gate [npc=23345]\n- Harfange the Black [npc=23933]\n- High Lorekeeper Udengar Dergon [npc=24018]\n- Lethar - second encounter [npc=23937]\n- Magmaraug [npc=23397]\n- Oblivion [npc=22461]\n- Obsidian [npc=22462]\n- Shrynn [npc=23567]\n- Slave Driver Azza [npc=23398]\n- Sulfurog [npc=23395]\n- a burly hill giant [npc=22469]\n- a worn jug [npc=23489]\n- age-old stones [npc=23392]\n- algae-covered stones [npc=23393]\n- an adult icewing [npc=23620]\n- an elder icewing [npc=22783]\n- ancient rocks [npc=23386]\n- discarded bones [npc=23383]\n- feathered fernstem [npc=23312]\n- forgotten bones [npc=23391]\n- moss-covered rocks [npc=23384]\n- old Tuffein lockbox [npc=23387]\n- pile of bones [npc=22930]\n- pile of dusty rocks [npc=23385]\n- rustling banebloom [npc=23394]\n- silverspun petals [npc=23389]\n- storage crate [npc=23388]\n- waving woodblossom [npc=23390]\n- where the red flower grows [npc=24286]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Fergarin Raid #2: Udengar the Traitor [quest=3954]\n**Era:** | !Serpents Spine\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Oct 4 22:42:13 2006\nModified: Sat Sep 7 01:26:11 2024 | | Find Librarian Hemfar on the first floor of Crescent Reach.\nYou say, 'Hail, Librarian Hemfar'\nLibrarian Hemfar says 'Vasha, friend. I am the second-born of Keikolin the Enlightened, the most knowledgeable dragon of the Six. I am to aid in the education of drakkin and all who choose to enlighten their minds. I am a collector of artifacts and one of the founders of the Written Word and the Wanderlust Guild so we may learn from books and life. I have a unique gift that you may partake in if you [aid] in my work. Or you may simply ask me what [lore] I have gathered from artifacts in these lands.\nYou say, 'Aid your work?'\nLibrarian Hemfar says 'Yes, indeed. I have been given a sight-gift from Lady Keikolin. In many artifacts I can see within them and through the eyes of those they belonged to. It allows me to create a history that will become part of this library. Should you find any artifacts in the surrounding lands, bring them to me and I shall reward you and be able to add to the [volumes] of our great library.'\nYou say, 'What volumes?'\nLibrarian Hemfar says 'There are many creatures present and past that lived in these mountains, including the ogres that once lived in this very city. What exactly happened to them and their kind is somewhat of a mystery, but given time and the right artifacts, we shall learn more. I can reward you if you bring artifacts to me. Then, you may ask what [lore] and legend is available as people bring me artifacts and I can share the history with you when it is scribed.'\n\n---\n\nThis is an ongoing quest to upgrade the charm, Serpent Seeker's Charm of Lore. After handing in at least five of the required items, you \"get an option that looks like it's the same old exp, but click the option and it shows charm as reward\".\nAs you hand in each of the following items from around the Serpent's Spine, the charm will increase in strength. It is not known which items boost stats, or how many are required for each increase. There does not appear to be any particular requirement for order, either. These are the items known to be involved. There are probably many more.\nItems used in this quest read \"This artifact might interest someone in Crescent Reach\" when the spell Identify is cast upon them.\nAshengate\n\\- Core of the Tyrant (dropped by Magmaraug in the west wing)\nAshengate, Reliquary of the Scale: North\n\\- Ebonheart of Lethar the Back (dropped by Lethar, second version)\n\\- Elddar Moonlocket (dropped by Dyn`Leth, Firstborn of Lethar)\nAshengate, Reliquary of the Scale: West\n\\- Ambersnout's Snout (dropped by Ambersnout the Aberration)\nCrescent Reach\n\\- Ancient Jewelry Box (/open the pile of bones behind the throne on third floor: -1225, -200)\n\\- Broken Nokk Insignia (/open discarded bones: +460, -2920)\n\\- Linguist's Note (a book on a table: second level of the inn, second door on the right, -1605, -1510)\nBlackfeather Roost\n\\- Silvered Blackfeather Plume (/open feathered fernstem: +2455, -1030)\nBlightfire Moors\n\\- Ancient Blighted Bark (/open moss-covered rocks: +610, -1275)\n\\- Murdunk's Rites Beads (/open pile of dusty rocks: +2060, -2060)\n\\- Petrified Leather Boot Sole (/open ancient rocks: +930, +45)\n\\- Preserved Hairy Halfling Foot (/open 'where the red flower grows': -1160, -2410 -- a flower amongst the vines)\nDirewind Cliffs\n\\- Gate Guardian Core (dropped by Guardian of the Gate)\n\\- Direwind Totem (dropped by Direwind Gust in Severan the Direwind Caller event)\nFrostcrypt: Raid Instance #2\n\\- Krithgorian Royal Crest (dropped by Harfange the Black)\n\\- Runed Sash of the Wraithguard (Dropped by Beltron the Shade King)\nGoru`kar Mesa\n\\- Cracked Waterspring Scepter (/open algae-covered stones: +1575, -45)\n\\- Devan's Feathered Arrow (/open age-old stones: -480, +1925)\n\\- Dromrek Worry Stone (quested from Shrynn: +1740, +2890)\n\\- Oread's Willow Whipvine (/open forgotten bones: -1155, +1970)\n\\- Sliver of Goru`kar's Willowstaff (/open waving woodblossom: -1070, +135)\n\\- Sparkling Windwillow Leaf (/open silverspun petals: -600, +30)\n\\- Split Ravenoak Bow (/open storage crate: +1050, -1160)\n\\- Thunderhorn of the Tribe (old Tuffein lockbox: -1510, -1095)\nIcefall Glacier\n\\- Cursed Lorekeeper's Quill (dropped by icewings)\n\\- Shattered Krithgor Keystone (ground spawn near spell vendors: -2035, -1155)\nStone Hive\n\\- Preserved Kithicor Baneleaf (/open rustling banebloom: +575, -775)\nSunderock Springs\n\\- Doomfount's Essence (dropped by Doomfount, an elemental who spawns at the geysers)\n\\- Elven Child's Vinewand (dropped by Slave Driver Azza in front of Vergalid Mines)\n\\- Lock of Veldyn's Hair (dropped by Obsidian)\n\\- Oblivion's Dark Core (dropped by Oblivion, raid encounter in northwest)\n\\- Relicstone Torch (dropped by Sulfurog: +2980, +1010)\n\\- Trinket of the Scale (dropped by Dranadune, a drake who spawns at the geysers)\nThe Steppes\n\\- Muddy Royal Scroll (dropped by burly hill giants)\n\\- Wulfnor Crown Gem (/open a worn jug: -1645, +800, inside a house with 3 mobs)\nValdeholm: Udengar the Traitor\n\\- Illegible Diary of Lorekeeper Baeldon (dropped by Lorekeeper Baeldon)\nVergalid Mines\n\\- Vergalid Scale (dropped by any undead golem)\nAfter completing all the non-raid areas except Vergalid Scale from Vergalid and Core of the Tyrant from Ashengate, you receive the title \"Cartographer.\"\nIt is also useful to do the tasks for the Wanderlust Guild [quest=3680] simultaneously.\n- Serpent Seeker's Charm of Lore [item=52354]",
